      ],
      "id": "rg4267d"
    },
    {
      "id": "ulnvush",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "g is maximum at poles and minimum at equator",
        "Gravitational force is always attractive in nature.It follows inverse square law (1/r²).",
        "A body floats when density of body &lt; density of liquid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hh01drx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MCQs"
    },
    {
      "id": "1ywddau",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q1."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "np0v9d2",
      "content": "Two masses 5 kg and 10 kg are separated by a distance of 2 m. The gravitational force between them (G = 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ N m²/kg²) is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4a3sejc",
      "content": "A) 8.3 × 10⁻¹¹ N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sai1o6c",
      "content": "B) 1.67 × 10⁻¹⁰ N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xv6d4wk",
      "content": "C) 3.33 × 10⁻¹⁰ N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qvnlcrn",
      "content": "D) 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m0qpqlf",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: A"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t8dbgox",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jthl3n0",
      "content": "Step 1: Use Newton’s Law of Gravitation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gqofska",
      "content": "F = G (m1 × m2) / r²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "71vuv9i",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute values."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f6krdsp",
      "content": "F = (6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ × 5 × 10) / (2²)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s44ldnj",
      "content": "F = (6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ × 50) / 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jx8v1mw",
      "content": "F = (333.5 × 10⁻¹¹) / 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "co5olat",
      "content": "F ≈ 8.3 × 10⁻¹⁰ N"
    },
    {
      "id": "cw1x11y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nafc2ct",
      "content": "A person has mass 60 kg. If acceleration due to gravity on Moon is 1.6 m/s², his weight on Moon is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "anoic8b",
      "content": "A) 96 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ygmnvum",
      "content": "B) 60 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7lb77r2",
      "content": "C) 588 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "fbfwe4f",
      "content": "D) 37.5 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "slu3usm",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: A"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ud53d3g",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "auqqmg7",
      "content": "Weight (W) = m × g"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ne3ikcq",
      "content": "W = 60 × 1.6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "cywe829",
      "content": "W = 96 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rfp4e2j",
      "content": "Note: Mass remains same everywhere."
    },
    {
      "id": "qcgtfh3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a2nkcoq",
      "content": "A stone is dropped from a height of 80 m (g = 10 m/s²). Time taken to reach ground is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "00vka1q",
      "content": "A) 2 s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xgot9f3",
      "content": "B) 4 s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bfttq8d",
      "content": "C) 8 s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "luv9thw",
      "content": "D) 16 s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wiv9q6r",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a9wexof",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iyc8fdn",
      "content": "Use formula: s = ½ g t²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lvfgh1z",
      "content": "80 = ½ × 10 × t²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jcom2tx",
      "content": "80 = 5t²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "15k360c",
      "content": "t² = 80/5 = 16"
    },
    {
